course: dictionary
lesson: 4188
title: Goo: sticky, soppy or baby talk
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Goo is a word with three different meanings. Read the words around it to find out which one the writer means.
explain: «The hagfish lets out slime that becomes a bucketful of goo in seconds.» Here goo is a sticky, wet, soft substance, like slime or glue. The words slime and bucketful are the clues.
explain: Goo can also mean too much soppy feeling, as in «romantic goo», or baby talk, as in «goo goo ga ga». Ask yourself: is it sticky, soppy or a baby's sound? Then put that meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
fact: Goo is an informal word, so you will hear it in everyday talk and stories more than in formal writing.
fact: «Goo» means a sticky, wet, soft substance, like slime, glue or melted cheese. The adjective is «gooey».
fact: «Goo» can also mean too much soppy, sentimental feeling, as in «romantic goo».
fact: «Goo goo ga ga» is baby talk. In science lessons, cornflour and water make a goo called oobleck, which acts like a solid when pressed and a liquid when poured.
exercise: «The hagfish lets out slime that becomes a bucketful of goo in seconds.» What is the goo here? | A kind of fish | *A sticky, wet, soft substance | Too much soppy feeling | Baby talk
exercise: Mia says the film had «romantic goo» in every scene. What does goo mean here? | Baby talk | A bucket of water | A sticky, wet, soft substance | *Too much soppy feeling
exercise: «The baby kept saying goo goo ga ga.» What is goo goo ga ga? | *Baby talk | A sticky substance | Slime made from cornflour | Soppy feelings
test: «Cornflour and water make a goo that is solid when pressed and runny when poured.» What does goo mean here? | A kind of biscuit | *A sticky, wet, soft substance | Too much soppy feeling | Baby talk
test: Which word is the adjective form of goo? | *gooey | goo | gooing | googly
exam: «The card was full of romantic goo, and everyone giggled.» What does goo mean here? | Melted cheese | A sticky substance | Baby talk | *Too much soppy feeling
